          "at": "2026-11-02T02:41:31.243Z",
          "html": "<p>Reworked and retitled \"6. Members Pages and Inbox\", with the same facts plus what had gone stale.  It now covers members' public spaces as well as inboxes, and most of it is tables.</p>\n<p><b>What was out of date:</b></p>\n<ul>\n  <li>It said only the person was on their inbox's list;  now it's the person, the Board and Admins.</li>\n  <li><code>owen@spell</code> is now <code>owen@rs</code>.</li>\n  <li>\"More private messages\" under Later suggested an inbox on the person's own host, which no longer fits, so it now only suggests encrypting messages.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><b>Two things I decided that you should check:</b></p>\n<ol>\n  <li><b>A member's own space holds documents and approved apps, not code they wrote.</b>  A page runs as the person viewing it, so a member's own code could read whatever that viewer can read.</li>\n  <li><b>A person's inbox stays with the org when they leave, and isn't offered to save.</b>  You may want their own messages to count as personal.</li>\n</ol>"
        }
      ],
